  "term": "outlier",
  "definition": "An outlier is a data point that is unusual or rare compared with the rest of the observations and lies far from the center of a distribution. Because there is no single agreed rule for identifying one, outliers should be interpreted cautiously and their impact on statistical results should be checked.",
